The comet was only detected at high phase angles, where forward scattering enhancement was pronounced, and its coma was detected in images taken in 2021 July and August, a few weeks from its perihelion passage. The detection of cometary activity is primarily caused by the brightness enhancement of the dust coma caused by forward scattering and/or enhanced activity at those epochs.

